hadiths[14]{hadithnumber,text}:
"353","On the laws of inheritance: Abu Kamil narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave the grandmother a sixth as sustenance."
"354","Abd al-Salam ibn Mutahhar narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave three grandmothers the sixth. I said: Who are they? He said: Your two grandmothers on your father's side, and your grandmother on your mother's side."
"355","Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, he said: I was told that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ... then he mentioned the like of it. (He said: So he asked) who are they? He said: The two grandmothers of the father: his father's mother and his mother's mother, and the grandmother of the mother: her mother's mother."
"356","Ubaydullah ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from al-Ash'ath, from al-Hasan, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave a grandmother the sixth, though her son was alive."
"357","Ibn al-Aswad narrated to us, Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, he said: The first grandmother to whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave sustenance was a father's mother, though her son was alive."
"358","Muhammad ibn Sulayman al-Anbari narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from al-Fadl ibn Dalham, from al-Hasan, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave three grandmothers inheritance."
"359","Isa ibn Yunus al-Tarsusi narrated to us, Hajjaj, meaning Ibn Muhammad, narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: An intentional or mistaken killer inherits nothing of the blood-money. Al-Zuhri said: He inherits from other than it. Abu Dawud said: Ma'mar, Salih ibn Kaysan and Yunus narrated the like from al-Zuhri, as the statement of Ibn al-Musayyib (mawquf)."
"360","Abdullah ibn Maslamah narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz, meaning Ibn Muhammad, narrated to us, from Zayd, meaning Ibn Aslam, from Ata', that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rode to Quba' seeking guidance (istikhara) concerning the inheritance of the paternal aunt and the maternal aunt, and it was revealed to him: There is no inheritance for them. Abu Dawud said: Its meaning is: They have no fixed share, but they inherit on account of kinship."
"361","Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abi Hind informed us, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Ubayd, from a man from the people of Sham, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The child of the woman subjected to li'an (mutual imprecation), his 'asabah (paternal heirs) are the 'asabah of his mother."
"362","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Habib ibn al-Shahid narrated to us, Humayd — meaning Ibn 'Abd al-Rahman — narrated to me, from al-Hasan ibn Salih, from 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Rufay', Abu Burdah ibn Abi Musa narrated to me, he said: A man died leaving his daughter and his manumitters, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) divided the property between them in two halves, between his daughter and his manumitters."
"363","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from 'Abdullah ibn Shaddad, that he said: Do you know what the daughter of Hamzah is to me? She was my sister through my mother, and she manumitted a slave of hers who then died leaving his daughter and his manumittress, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed his inheritance between them in halves. Abu Dawud said: Several narrated it from 'Abdullah ibn Shaddad, that the daughter of Hamzah was the one who manumitted."
"364","Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, from Khalid, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, he said: A freed slave of Hamzah ibn 'Abd al-Muttalib died, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave the daughter of Hamzah half and took (the other) half. Al-Husayn ibn 'Ali ibn al-Aswad narrated to us, Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Sharik said: Ibrahim ventured rashly into this statement, unless he heard something and narrated it, and he narrated little."
"365","Husayn ibn 'Ali ibn al-Aswad narrated to us, Yahya — meaning Ibn Adam — narrated to us, 'Abd al-Salam — meaning Ibn Harb — narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from 'Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr and others, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married 'Umarah bint Hamzah to Salamah ibn Abi Salamah though they had not reached maturity, then they died and inherited from one another."
"366","Musaddad narrated to us, 'Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated to us, from Habib ibn al-Mu'allim, from al-Hasan, that a man from the polytheists went out performing Hajj, and when he returned departing, a Muslim man met him and killed him, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him to pay his blood-money to his family."
